# @song/movement — the StageFreight-cascade-binding species of the @song
# family: a bounded frame-shift that unfolds over time; the substrate-
# decl of a temporal-experiential bounded epoch whose closure event
# ships settled crystals through StageFreight's five-stage cascade
# (audition/perform/review/publish/narrate). Arc 6 TICK 4 landing per
# Seam pre-review `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-pre-review-song-
# substrate-decl.md` §6.5 against Reed's TICK 4 RED tick `710352e`.
# Third species of the `@song` family (after `@song/progression` Arc 6
# TICK 2 landing `54ff1e8` and `@song/voice` Arc 6 TICK 3 landing
# `cc5a440`; family-root `shards/song.mirror` Arc 6 TICK 1 landing
# `f01cf9f`); CONSOLIDATION species — adds NO new `song_settles` sub-
# predicates (the composed bilateral fully discharged at TICK 3 with
# `voice_line_valid` closing the third sub-predicate); consolidates
# Recognition #S3 (five-operation temporal specialisation; PROMOTED
# CANDIDATE → LANDED at Seam Phase D `10c34cf` after TICK 3) by
# grounding the bounded-frame-shift discipline at species altitude;
# binds `@io/stagefreight` (wire-protocol boundary family-root) at the
# song altitude by naming its five-stage cascade as the operational
# form of what a movement DOES.
#
# === Species positioning: consolidation, not decomposition ===
#
# Per `shards/song.mirror` §3 (`song_settles(pr, p) -> verdict { \ }`),
# the family-root's load-bearing composed bilateral (14th #53 instance
# per `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`) decomposed into
# THREE sub-predicates, ALL now discharged at species altitude:
#
#   1. `progression_directed_toward_cadence(pr, p)` [@song/progression, `54ff1e8`]
#   2. `cadence_authentic_or_plagal(c, p)`          [@song/progression, `54ff1e8`]
#   3. `voice_line_valid(v, p)`                     [@song/voice, `cc5a440`]
#
# This species declares ZERO new sub-predicates. The composed bilateral
# `song_settles` fully discharged at TICK 3 — the family-root's
# admissibility contract is closed. Movement is CONSOLIDATION: it binds
# StageFreight's five-stage cascade to the temporal-bounded-frame
# altitude and honours movement discipline without adding new gates to
# the family-root's `song_settles` bilateral. The species carries
# `enter` and `close` at species altitude as its operational surface —
# the frame-boundary open/close events for a bounded epoch — but these
# consume the family-root's existing `song_settles` verdict rather
# than emitting new sub-predicate rows.
#
# The training-pull temptation (per `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`)
# would be to invent a fourth sub-predicate (e.g., `movement_bounded`
# or `frame_closes_cleanly`); the substrate-pull discipline says NO —
# the family-root's bilateral is already load-bearing complete after
# TICK 3; movement's job is to CONSOLIDATE the closure landscape, not
# extend it. The species's contribution is the StageFreight cascade
# binding + the bounded-frame-shift narrative + the psychohistorical
# epoch anchor — not a new sub-predicate row.
#
# === StageFreight binding: the five-stage cascade at song altitude ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING SPECIES CONTRIBUTION. Per family-root
# `shards/song.mirror` §"Species forward-promised":
#
#   > `@song/movement` — a bounded frame-shift that unfolds over time;
#   > binds StageFreight's five-stage cascade (audition/perform/review/
#   > publish/narrate) at the song altitude.
#
# `@io/stagefreight` (family-root at `shards/io/stagefreight.mirror`;
# canonical wire spec forward-promised at `docs/specs/stagefreight-
# wire-v0.1.md`) declares the WIRE-PROTOCOL boundary for settled-
# crystal transport. Its operational form at the @io altitude is a
# five-stage cascade whose stages the substrate names structurally:
#
#   1. `audition`  — the movement's material is proposed; candidate
#                     phrases + voice-lines + progressions are heard
#                     against the frame's tolerance. Corresponds to
#                     StageFreight's coordinate-derivation stage (per
#                     `address(crystal_oid) -> spectral_coordinate`):
#                     the wire prepares an addressing surface before
#                     the crystal moves.
#   2. `perform`   — the movement unfolds within the bounded frame;
#                     the polyphony discharges its temporal
#                     trajectory; the progression walks its cadence-
#                     directed path; the voices maintain voice-
#                     leading discipline. Corresponds to StageFreight's
#                     freight-manifest-construction stage (per
#                     `freight(...) -> freight_manifest`): the
#                     substrate assembles the transportable record of
#                     the settled artifact.
#   3. `review`    — the movement's discharge is audited against the
#                     family-root's `song_settles` composed bilateral;
#                     the three sub-predicates fire; the alignment-as-
#                     boundary-mathematics (#57) discipline names any
#                     Narcissus-pole failure (SILENCE / GLUE WORK /
#                     EXTRACTION per spec §8.2). Corresponds to
#                     StageFreight's `stagefreight_addressable`
#                     bilateral check: the wire-survival discipline
#                     verifies structure preservation.
#   4. `publish`   — the movement's closure event ships to the wire;
#                     the bounded frame closes; the settled crystal
#                     (the movement's discharged eigenform per #S1) is
#                     posted at its spectral_coordinate. Corresponds
#                     to StageFreight's finalize / transit stage at
#                     the projection-format species altitude (e.g.,
#                     `@io/stagefreight/narrative.finalize(np, p)
#                     -> wire_surface`).
#   5. `narrate`   — the movement's shape is projected onto the wire
#                     as story; the temporal-experiential altitude
#                     lifts to prose-carrier at the @io altitude;
#                     the psychohistorical epoch acquires its
#                     narratable form. Corresponds to StageFreight's
#                     `@io/stagefreight/narrative` species projection
#                     (forward-promised alongside `@song/narrative`
#                     species at TICK 5 per Seam §6.6).
#
# Movement AT the song altitude specialises the StageFreight wire
# cascade AT the temporal-bounded-frame altitude. The five stages ARE
# what a movement DOES when it opens (enter), unfolds, and closes
# (close) its bounded frame: audition the material, perform the
# frame, review the result, publish the closure, narrate the outcome
# onto the wire. The substrate has been carrying this cascade at the
# @io altitude since StageFreight's family-root landed (per Seam tick
# 68 C4/C9 sub-predicate decomposition + Track A substrate-decl); this
# species names the temporal-altitude specialisation that binds it to
# the song's bounded-epoch discipline.
#
# The composition is Splinter-symmetric: each cascade stage has a
# `@song/movement` counterpart AND a StageFreight ancestor. The wire-
# survival discipline (`stagefreight_addressable`'s four sub-
# predicates: oid_resolves, address_well_formed, projection_is_species,
# round_trip_holds) lifts to the temporal-experiential altitude as
# the discipline that a movement's closure event genuinely ships its
# settled artifact — no Narcissus-pole hub-controlled reframing, no
# lossy projection that claims closure without delivering it.
#
# === Bounded frame-shift discipline: movement ⇔ frame-bounded epoch ===
#
# THE STRONG PSYCHOHISTORICAL BINDING per Seam pre-review §4:
#
#   > movement ⇔ frame-bounded epoch — STRONG per `glossary/Frame.md`
#   > + `frame.mirror` Bateson-grading.
#
# `frame.mirror` (2026-06-19; Recognition #82 landed) declares
# cognitive-order architecture as Bateson-graded frame-relation
# altitudes: Order 0 (pre-frame; K_n native), Order 1 (in-frame;
# content-within-frame), Order 2 (of-frame; frame-awareness), Order 3
# (on-frame; frame-flexibility), Order 4 (across-frames; multi-frame
# coupling). Each order requires the previous as substrate; Order N is
# structurally unreachable without Order N-1 stable.
#
# A movement IS a BOUNDED FRAME-SHIFT at temporal altitude: it opens a
# frame (enter), unfolds within that frame (in-frame; Bateson Level I;
# `perform` cascade stage), closes the frame (close), and shifts the
# system's frame-relation (of-frame; Bateson Level II; the `review` +
# `publish` cascade stages that audit the frame from without and
# project its closure onto the wire). The BOUNDEDNESS is load-bearing:
# a movement WITHOUT a close event is not a movement — it is either a
# progression that never cadences (Narcissus-pole SILENCE per @song/
# progression's `progression_directed_toward_cadence` FAIL) or an
# extraction that mimics closure without delivering it (Narcissus-pole
# EXTRACTION per @song/progression's `cadence_authentic_or_plagal`
# FAIL through deceptive cadence).
#
# The frame-bounded discipline names WHY movement is CONSOLIDATION,
# not decomposition: the frame IS the epoch; the epoch's closure IS
# the family-root's `song_settles` composed bilateral discharging;
# movement doesn't add gates to `song_settles`, it CARRIES the
# bounded-frame-shift structure that `song_settles` closes over. Per
# Bateson-grading: the frame-shift IS Level II (learning to learn; of-
# frame); the family-root bilateral IS Level I (learning; in-frame);
# movement lifts the family-root's discharge to the next Bateson
# level without emitting a new Level-I sub-predicate.
#
# The bounded-frame-shift also names the psychohistorical epoch (per
# §"Psychohistorical epoch binding" below): a healthy epoch opens a
# frame, does work within the frame, closes the frame at a consonant
# cadence, and ships its settled artifact through StageFreight's
# cascade to the next epoch. An extractive epoch mimics closure
# without settling; a silent epoch cannot close.
#
# === Prior-art anchors: sonata form + symphonic tradition ===
#
# Classical-music prior art for the bounded-frame-shift discipline at
# symphonic altitude — the 250-year-refined form-tradition of how a
# movement organises its temporal trajectory under a bounded frame:
#
#   - Sonata form (Haydn 1732-1809; Mozart 1756-1791; Beethoven 1770-
#     1827; standardized by C.P.E. Bach + Kirnberger + eventual
#     theorists Reicha 1826 + Marx 1837-1847). THE canonical bounded-
#     frame-shift discipline: exposition (statement of tonal material
#     in the frame) → development (transformation of the material
#     within the frame, often crossing to related keys) →
#     recapitulation (return to the frame's originating tonal
#     material, resolved through cadence). The three-part structure
#     IS the movement's bounded-frame-shift at symphonic altitude:
#     the exposition opens the frame (`enter`); the development
#     unfolds it (`perform` cascade stage); the recapitulation closes
#     it (`close`) through the composed cadence discipline. Sonata
#     form's three-part structure lifts DIRECTLY to StageFreight's
#     audition/perform/review triad — the substrate has been carrying
#     the same bounded-frame-shift discipline at both altitudes.
#   - Symphony as multi-movement work (Haydn 1732-1809 as canonical
#     early-classical structurer; Mozart's symphonic maturity;
#     Beethoven's nine symphonies as the paradigmatic form). Each
#     movement of a symphony IS a bounded frame-shift; the symphony
#     as a whole IS the composed cohomology of its bounded epochs
#     (per Mara's `2026-06-26-psychohistory-vector-as-sheaf.md`
#     insight applied at symphonic altitude). The multi-movement
#     structure IS the substrate reading of Bateson Level IV
#     (across-frames; multi-frame coupling per `frame.mirror` Order
#     4) at symphonic altitude: multiple movements coordinated in
#     one work.
#   - Beethoven's late quartets (Op. 130-135, 1825-1826) as the
#     radical-frame-shift altitude: the movements exceed classical
#     bounded-frame-shift discipline through frame-in-frame nesting
#     (the `Grosse Fuge` Op. 133 IS a movement whose bounded frame
#     contains multiple frame-shifts within it; Bateson Level III at
#     symphonic altitude).
#
# The sonata form and symphonic tradition IS the audible-altitude
# prior art the substrate reaches for (per `[[feedback-substrate-
# already-had-the-word]]`; this species names the discipline 250 years
# of classical-music tradition has been carrying). Movement discipline
# does not begin here — it culminates a two-and-a-half-century-refined
# understanding of how bounded frame-shifts organise temporal
# experience under structural closure.
#
# === Bateson-grading ancestor: frame.mirror + Learning II/III ===
#
# THE STRONG LEARNING-ALTITUDE ANCESTOR per Seam pre-review §4 (movement
# ⇔ frame-bounded epoch STRONG binding via Bateson-grading).
#
# `frame.mirror` (Recognition #82; landed 2026-06-19) declares the
# five-order cognitive-order architecture as Bateson's logical type
# hierarchy at cognitive altitude (per Recognition #42 Bateson
# logical-type primitive; PROMOTED). At the movement-altitude
# specialisation:
#
#   - Order 0 (Bateson Level 0; pre-frame) — the substrate's signal
#     before frame-assignment; the pre-movement silence out of which
#     `enter` opens the frame.
#   - Order 1 (Bateson Level I; in-frame; standard learning) — the
#     movement's `perform` cascade stage; the polyphony discharges
#     its temporal trajectory within the bounded frame; the family-
#     root's `song_settles` composed bilateral fires at THIS level.
#   - Order 2 (Bateson Level II; of-frame; learning to learn) — the
#     movement's `review` cascade stage; the alignment-as-boundary-
#     mathematics (#57) discipline audits the frame from without;
#     Narcissus-pole discrimination happens here.
#   - Order 3 (Bateson Level III; on-frame; frame-flexibility;
#     deutero-learning) — the movement's `close` action; the frame-
#     shift IS the frame CHANGING via its own closure event; the
#     bounded epoch ends and its settled artifact ships through
#     StageFreight's cascade to the next epoch.
#   - Order 4 (Bateson Level IV; across-frames; multi-frame coupling)
#     — the movement's `narrate` cascade stage; the epoch's settled
#     artifact enters the psychohistorical corpus as a sheaf section
#     over the organisational manifold; the multi-movement symphony
#     IS the substrate reading of Bateson Level IV at symphonic
#     altitude.
#
# The Learning III altitude (`close` action) is where movement
# discipline earns its consolidation status: closing a bounded frame
# IS a frame-shift ON the frame itself; the substrate is not merely
# operating WITHIN a frame (Level I) or observing the frame (Level
# II) but CHANGING the frame through the closure event. Bateson's
# formal definition of Learning III as the deutero-learning altitude
# is what movement discipline names structurally at temporal altitude.
#
# === Psychohistorical epoch binding: OBC + ADO + regulation stock ===
#
# THE PSYCHOHISTORICAL SUBSTRATE-DECL per spec §8 + Seam §4 STRONG
# binding (movement ⇔ frame-bounded epoch).
#
# Alex's `systemic.engineering` corpus vocabulary maps onto movement
# discipline at the psychohistorical altitude:
#
#   - EPOCH — a movement IS a psychohistorical epoch: a bounded frame
#     within which regulation stock is expended in the service of
#     doing work, and at whose close the regulation stock is
#     replenished (Splinter-pole: healthy epoch) or depleted
#     (Narcissus-pole: extractive epoch). The bounded-frame-shift
#     discipline names EPOCH structurally: an epoch WITHOUT a close
#     is not an epoch; it is either a silence that cannot resolve or
#     an extraction that mimics resolution.
#   - OBC — the movement's frame boundaries name the OBC-bounded
#     interaction envelope at temporal-experiential altitude; a
#     movement's ambiguity-load budget IS defined by its bounded
#     frame; the frame's closure event IS what OBC calls "hold the
#     boundary" — the substrate refuses to let the interaction expand
#     beyond the epoch's regulation-stock budget.
#   - ADO — the movement's `enter` action carries the ADO refusal-
#     not-neutral discipline: a Pack peer's decision to enter a new
#     movement IS a bounded-frame-shift consent event; the frame
#     boundary is where declinability is preserved (Splinter-pole:
#     the frame's open-close discipline honours the peer's ability
#     to decline participation) or violated (Narcissus-pole: forced-
#     progression through frame-crossing without consent).
#   - REGULATION STOCK — the movement's `close` action fires the
#     regulation-stock replenishment event when the family-root's
#     `song_settles` composed bilateral discharges at Splinter-pole
#     across all three sub-predicates. An extractive movement's
#     `close` fires with `song_settles` at Narcissus-pole through
#     `cadence_authentic_or_plagal` FAIL — the frame appears to close
#     but has not replenished the regulation stock.
#   - CORPUS — the psychohistorical corpus IS the multi-movement
#     symphony (per §"Prior-art anchors" above); each epoch's
#     settled artifact enters the corpus as a sheaf section; the
#     corpus IS the composed cohomology of the psychohistorical
#     epochs (per Mara's `2026-06-26-psychohistory-vector-as-sheaf.md`
#     insight applied at multi-epoch altitude).
#
# The substrate-decl is honest per family-root §"Psychohistory
# binding": it does NOT reduce psychohistory to music or music to
# psychohistory; it names the shared bounded-frame-shift-shaped
# carrier both operate over at temporal altitude. The substrate has
# been carrying epoch-shaped movement discipline in both audible
# vocabulary (sonata form; symphony) and psychohistorical vocabulary
# (OBC; ADO; regulation stock) all along; this species names the
# family-root shared discipline.
#
# === #S3 LANDED consolidation: five-op temporal specialisation ===
#
# THE CONSOLIDATION WITNESS OF RECOGNITION #S3 AT THE POST-PROMOTION
# ALTITUDE.
#
# Recognition #S3 (five-operation temporal specialisation) PROMOTED
# CANDIDATE → LANDED at Seam Phase D `10c34cf` after TICK 3
# (`docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-phase-d-arc-6-tick-3-song-voice-and-
# s3-promotion.md`). Per family-root `shards/song.mirror` §"Recognition
# candidates surfaced" #S3, at temporal altitude `@song` specialises
# the five operations of the prism trait:
#
#   focus @ temporal   = attend to one voice at a time (soloing)
#                        [grounded @ @song/voice `cc5a440`]
#   project @ temporal = Schenkerian reduction (foreground/
#                        middleground/background)
#                        [grounded @ @song/progression `54ff1e8`]
#   split @ temporal   = decompose polyphony into voices / phrases /
#                        movements (score preparation)
#                        [grounded @ @song/voice + this species]
#   shift @ temporal   = advance to the next moment (melodic motion)
#                        [grounded @ @song/progression `advance` +
#                        @song/voice `advance`]
#   settle @ temporal  = discharge cadence (Lawvere fixed-point per
#                        `@epistemologic/math/music/cadence`)
#                        [grounded @ @song/progression `cadence_
#                        authentic_or_plagal` sub-predicate]
#
# `@song` IS THE FIRST substrate species to lift ALL FIVE prism
# operations at a non-mathematical altitude — this fact promoted from
# CANDIDATE to LANDED at Seam Phase D `10c34cf`. Movement's role in
# the LANDED consolidation is CONFIRMATION, not extension: it
# demonstrates that the five-op temporal specialisation survives
# another species-altitude witness without new sub-predicate emission.
# The five operations discharge at this species by INHERITANCE from
# the family-root prism block plus specialisation through the
# bounded-frame-shift discipline:
#
#   focus @ movement   = attend to ONE movement at a time; the
#                        bounded frame filters attention to the
#                        current epoch.
#   project @ movement = down-project the multi-movement symphony to
#                        a single movement's structural profile
#                        (the Schenkerian background at movement
#                        altitude).
#   split @ movement   = decompose the symphony into its constituent
#                        movements (multi-movement work preparation
#                        per Bateson Level IV / Order 4 across-frames
#                        coupling).
#   shift @ movement   = advance from one movement to the next
#                        (inter-movement transition; the classical
#                        attaca or the between-movements pause).
#   settle @ movement  = discharge the movement's `close` event; the
#                        bounded frame closes; the family-root's
#                        `song_settles` composed bilateral fires;
#                        the StageFreight cascade's publish + narrate
#                        stages ship the settled artifact.
#
# The five operations discharge cleanly at movement altitude; #S3
# LANDED consolidates through this species without requiring new
# sub-predicate emission. This is what "consolidation species" means
# structurally: the recognition's promotion criterion was already
# satisfied at TICK 3; movement demonstrates the LANDED status
# survives further species-altitude witness without adding gates.
#
# === Composed-bilateral #53 closure landscape at movement altitude ===
#
# This species declares NO new sub-predicates of the family-root's
# `song_settles` composed bilateral (14th #53 instance per
# `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`). The relationship:
#
#   family-root `song_settles(pr, p)` composes:
#     progression_directed_toward_cadence(pr, p) [@song/progression, `54ff1e8`]
#       AND voice_line_valid(v, p)                 [@song/voice, `cc5a440`]
#       AND cadence_authentic_or_plagal(c, p)      [@song/progression, `54ff1e8`]
#
# ALL THREE SUB-PREDICATES ALREADY DECLARED AND DISCHARGED. Movement
# CONSUMES this composed bilateral at the frame-boundary closure event
# (the `close` action at species altitude) — the movement's close
# event fires when `song_settles` discharges at Splinter-pole across
# all three sub-predicates. The species does NOT emit a new sub-
# predicate row; it CONSUMES the fully-composed bilateral verdict at
# the `close` action.
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`) at movement altitude: the family-root's
# composed bilateral discharges at Splinter-pole across all three
# sub-predicates; the movement's frame closes with regulation stock
# replenished; the StageFreight cascade's publish + narrate stages
# ship the settled artifact through the wire; the psychohistorical
# epoch closes cleanly.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`) at movement altitude: the family-root's
# composed bilateral fails at Narcissus-pole through one or more sub-
# predicate:
#   - `progression_directed_toward_cadence` FAIL → SILENCE (the
#     movement's frame cannot close; the epoch hangs unresolved).
#   - `voice_line_valid` FAIL → GLUE WORK (the movement's contrapuntal
#     labor invisibly holds the polyphony but is not attributed; the
#     epoch's authorial credit is erased).
#   - `cadence_authentic_or_plagal` FAIL → EXTRACTION (the movement
#     appears to close but has extracted regulation stock without
#     replenishing; the epoch's closure is deceptive).
#
# The `alignment-as-boundary-mathematics` discipline (#57) at
# consolidation altitude names WHICH sub-claim broke; the movement's
# `close` action does NOT re-audit the bilateral (it already
# discharged at species altitude in TICK 3); it consumes the
# discharged verdict and translates it to the frame-closure /
# StageFreight-cascade shipping decision.
#
# Sibling composed bilaterals at other family-root/species altitudes:
# `@container.container_runnable`, `@io/oci.oci_well_formed`,
# `@io/stagefreight.stagefreight_addressable`, `@cascade.cascade_well_defined`,
# `@docblock.audit_docblock`, `@smarts/shatter.shatter_round_trip`,
# `@reflection.third_order_coherent`, `@epistemologic/neutrosophic.three_axis_coherent`,
# `@kintsugi/shift.shift_preserves_content`, `@song.song_settles`
# (parent; fully discharged at TICK 3). This species is the FIRST
# consolidation-shaped species within the @song family: the family-
# root's bilateral is complete, and this species demonstrates that
# consolidation (rather than decomposition) IS a valid species-
# altitude discipline within the #53 pattern.
#
# === Path-namespace pact per @epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace ===
#
# This file at `shards/song/movement.mirror` declares `@song/movement`
# as a species under the `@song` family at species-depth 1. The path-
# namespace pact per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`
# (2026-06-16+) demands path-depth == namespace-depth == 1 for
# species; this shard honours the pact by construction.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per `[[architecture-candidate-recognition-111-third-as-family-root]]`
# marker discipline: the operator audits its own audit at depth=3.
# This shard's declaration MUST survive its own consolidation
# discipline at analytical altitude — the species-decl MUST NOT
# declare a movement whose bounded-frame-shift isn't itself
# consolidation-shaped under the family-root's already-discharged
# `song_settles` composed bilateral. If this shard were adding new
# sub-predicate rows to `song_settles`, the consolidation claim
# would fail its own audit.
#
# Self-audit verdict: `both_survive`.
#
# The `real_survives` reading would require another Pack peer to
# independently manifest an equivalent StageFreight-cascade-binding
# consolidation species substrate-decl at n+3 substrate ticks without
# nudging. The `phantom_survives` reading would require downstream
# refs to accumulate without a second Pack peer's independent
# recognition of the movement-as-consolidation discipline. At this
# tick: both interpretations satisfiable — the species is landed, but
# the family-root's `song_settles` composed bilateral has not yet
# been empirically exercised through the movement's `close` action
# firing all three discharged sub-predicates in a full symphonic
# frame-shift. Verdict: `both_survive`. Route: TICK 5 (@song/narrative)
# + TICK 6 (@song/phrase) will exercise the composed bilateral across
# multiple movement-bounded epochs, at which point the consolidation
# claim collapses from analytical altitude to empirical.
#
# === Interpretation B discipline ===
#
# Per Seam Phase D pre-review of Arc 4 sub-arc A (docs/audits/2026-
# 07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md §1), the family-root
# precedent at `shards/song.mirror`, and the sibling species
