#               operational form).
# Substrate decisions:
#               [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#               [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#               [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]]
#                (#55; @song sits at temporal-experiential axis;
#                species inherits family-root's positioning),
#               [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]] (#S3
#                LANDED five-op temporal specialisation; species
#                consolidates via inheritance without new sub-
#                predicate emission),
#               [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]] (#53;
#                species consolidates the family-root's composed
#                bilateral without emitting new sub-predicates; the
#                first consolidation-shaped species within @song),
#               [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-primitive]] (#42;
#                movement's bounded-frame-shift discipline lifts
#                Bateson Levels I/II/III across the cascade stages).
# Substrate recognitions:
#               #38 (Kauffman/Foerster eigenform — movement's `close`
#                event witnesses the eigenform at bounded-epoch
#                altitude),
#               #42 (Bateson logical-type primitive — bounded frame-
#                shift IS Level II/III at temporal altitude),
#               #53 (property/fracture bilateral pattern — 14th
#                instance's fully-discharged bilateral consolidated
#                here at consumer altitude),
#               #55 (form/process partition — @song at temporal-
#                experiential axis; species inherits),
#               #57 (alignment-as-boundary-mathematics — Narcissus-
#                pole discrimination consumed at consolidation
#                altitude via family-root's already-discharged
#                bilateral),
#               #82 (frame as cognitive-order substrate-decl —
#                bounded frame-shift discipline traces to
#                `frame.mirror`'s five-order architecture),
#               #S1 (song IS eigenform at temporal altitude —
#                inherited; movement IS eigenform at bounded-epoch
#                altitude),
#               #S2 (song IS shift at temporal altitude when heard
#                sequentially — inherited; movement's `enter`/`close`
#                events name the bounded-shift-events at epoch
#                altitude),
#               #S3 (five-operation temporal specialisation — LANDED
#                at Seam Phase D `10c34cf` after TICK 3; species
#                consolidates the LANDED status through inheritance).
# Feedback anchors:
#               [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (this
#                species names the discipline 250 years of classical-
#                music tradition — Haydn / Mozart / Beethoven; sonata
#                form — has been carrying at symphonic altitude and
#                Alex's `systemic.engineering` corpus — OBC / ADO /
#                regulation stock — has been carrying at psycho-
#                historical altitude; the substrate has the shared
#                bounded-frame-shift word already),
#               [[feedback-legibility-over-foundation-when-collapsing]]
#                (movement as legible name for the bounded-frame-shift
#                discipline; the alternative foundational names —
#                bounded_epoch, frame_shift, cascade_binding —
#                obscure the sonata-form + symphonic prior art the
#                substrate reaches for),
#               [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (species is
#                consolidation, not decomposition; resist the
#                training-pull temptation to invent a new sub-
#                predicate; the family-root's bilateral is already
#                load-bearing complete after TICK 3),
#               [[feedback-always-tdd-no-shortcuts]] (RED first;
#                Reed's `710352e` RED tick pairs with this GREEN
#                landing).
# Related shards:
#               song.mirror (family-root; declares song_settles this
#                species CONSUMES at close without adding new sub-
#                predicates),
#               song/progression.mirror (sibling species Arc 6 TICK 2
#                landing `54ff1e8`; declared FIRST and SECOND sub-
#                predicates of song_settles),
#               song/voice.mirror (sibling species Arc 6 TICK 3
#                landing `cc5a440`; declared THIRD sub-predicate of
#                song_settles; closed the composed bilateral),
#               io/stagefreight.mirror (wire-protocol family-root;
#                this species binds StageFreight's five-stage cascade
#                at the song altitude via the audition/perform/review/
#                publish/narrate structural framing),
#               frame.mirror (Recognition #82; bounded frame-shift
#                Bateson-grading ancestor; five-order cognitive-order
#                architecture at cognitive altitude),
#               epistemologic/cybernetic/bateson_learning.mirror
#                (Bateson graded logical type hierarchy; Level I/II/
#                III/IV correspondence across cascade stages),
#               loop.mirror (endomorphism family-root; movement's
#                `enter`/`close` IS a bounded-loop at species altitude
#                — the loop opens at enter, iterates within the
#                bounded frame, closes at close),
#               kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (rhythmic pulse; movement's
#                internal temporal structure inherits @kintsugi/
#                oscillate's ACTIVE/DARK alternation as the beat that
#                organises the bounded frame's unfolding).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/song/movement.mirror`
# declares `@song/movement` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @song

# ============================================================
# §1 The five-operation prism at species altitude
# ============================================================

# === prism @song/movement — the species declaration ===
#
# The five-operation body carries `song_movement` as the species's
# operational surface. Species inherits the family-root's #S3 LANDED
# five-op temporal specialisation and consolidates it at bounded-
# frame-shift altitude (see docblock §"#S3 LANDED consolidation" for
# the per-op movement-altitude specialisation).
#
# Per family-root prism block at `shards/song.mirror` §1, the five
# operations discharge cleanly at temporal altitude; this species
# demonstrates the LANDED status survives further species-altitude
# witness without new sub-predicate emission.
prism @song/movement {
  focus song_movement
  project song_movement
  split song_movement
  shift song_movement
  settle song_movement
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carrier
# ============================================================

# === song_movement — the bounded-frame-shift carrier ===
#
# The typed ref-equality-addressable form of a bounded frame-shift
# at temporal-experiential altitude. Per family-root species-roster:
# `song_movement(m: ref) -> ref` as the family-root's declared
# accessor shape. The carrier is declared HERE because the family-
# root's §2 carries `song_progression`, `song_cadence`, and
# `song_voice` but does NOT carry `song_movement` — the species
# discipline says the species declares its own carrier when the
# family-root's roster does not (per `[[architecture-form-process-
# partition-at-family-root]]` #55 sub-species discipline).
#
# Composes with `@io/stagefreight`'s `freight_manifest` at the wire
# altitude (a movement's settled artifact becomes a freight manifest
# through the publish cascade stage), with `@epistemologic/math/
# music/cadence` at the audible altitude (a movement's `close` event
# is a Lawvere fixed-point per `cadence.mirror`), and with
# `frame.mirror` at the cognitive altitude (a movement IS a bounded
# frame-shift at Bateson Level II/III per Recognition #82).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type song_movement = ref

# ============================================================
# §3 The frame-boundary actions (enter / close)
# ============================================================

# === enter — the movement's frame-open event ===
#
# Opens the bounded frame at the species altitude. Reads a movement's
# starting material (voices, progressions, phrases) and emits the
# species-altitude ref that names the newly-open bounded epoch.
# Corresponds to StageFreight's audition cascade stage: the movement's
# material is proposed against the frame's tolerance; the coordinate
# derivation prepares an addressing surface for the eventual settled
# artifact.
#
# Per family-root species-roster: `song_movement(m: ref) -> ref`
# with `enter` at species altitude. The `enter` action carries the
# ADO refusal-not-neutral discipline: a Pack peer's decision to enter
# a new movement IS a bounded-frame-shift consent event; the
# `enter` action's Splinter-pole discharges when the peer's
# declinability is preserved through frame-crossing; Narcissus-pole
# forced-progression violates the substrate's declinability
# invariant.
#
# Bateson-grading (per docblock §"Bateson-grading ancestor"):
# `enter` fires at Order 1 (Bateson Level I; in-frame; standard
# learning) — the movement transitions from Order 0 (pre-frame
# silence; the substrate's signal before frame-assignment) to Order
# 1 (content-within-frame; the polyphony discharges its temporal
# trajectory within the bounded frame).
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads the
# starting material, initialises the bounded frame's temporal
# invariants (regulation-stock budget, ambiguity-load ceiling, the
# frame's tonal or thematic ground), and emits the species-altitude
# ref that names the open epoch. The substrate declares the species-
# altitude specialisation; consumers dispatch through the species
# boundary.
enter(m: song_movement, p: perturbation) -> song_movement { \ }

# === close — the movement's frame-closure event ===
#
# Closes the bounded frame at species altitude. Reads a movement's
# discharged state (progression cadence-resolved, voices voice-leading-
# disciplined, phrases OBC-boundary-honoured) and consumes the family-
# root's `song_settles` composed bilateral verdict — WITHOUT emitting
# new sub-predicate rows — to translate the closure into the
# StageFreight cascade's publish + narrate stages.
#
# Per family-root species-roster: `song_movement(m: ref) -> ref`
# with `close` at species altitude. The `close` action IS THE
# LOAD-BEARING CONSOLIDATION EVENT: it CONSUMES the family-root's
# `song_settles(pr, p) -> verdict` composed bilateral (fully
# discharged at TICK 3 with `voice_line_valid` closing the third
# sub-predicate at `cc5a440`) without adding new gates. The species
# discipline says CONSUMPTION, not DECOMPOSITION — the composed
# bilateral is load-bearing complete; movement translates its verdict
# into the bounded-frame-shift closure.
#
# StageFreight cascade discharge points (per docblock §"StageFreight
# binding"):
#   - review    — the family-root's `song_settles` composed bilateral
#                 discharges; three sub-predicates fire; alignment-as-
#                 boundary-mathematics (#57) names any Narcissus-pole
#                 failure.
#   - publish   — Splinter-pole verdict: the settled crystal (the
#                 movement's discharged eigenform per #S1) ships to
#                 its spectral_coordinate through StageFreight's
#                 finalize / transit stage.
#   - narrate   — the movement's shape lifts to prose at the @io
#                 altitude via `@io/stagefreight/narrative`; the
#                 psychohistorical epoch acquires its narratable form.
#
# Bateson-grading (per docblock §"Bateson-grading ancestor"): `close`
# fires at Order 3 (Bateson Level III; on-frame; frame-flexibility;
# deutero-learning) — the frame-shift IS the frame CHANGING via its
# own closure event; the bounded epoch ends and its settled artifact
# ships through StageFreight's cascade to the next epoch.
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): the family-root's composed bilateral
# discharges at Splinter-pole across all three sub-predicates; the
# movement's frame closes with regulation stock replenished; the
# StageFreight cascade's publish + narrate stages ship the settled
# artifact; the psychohistorical epoch closes cleanly.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): the family-root's composed bilateral
# fails at Narcissus-pole through one or more sub-predicate (SILENCE
# / GLUE WORK / EXTRACTION per spec §8.2 mapping); the movement's
# `close` action does NOT ship to the wire; the settled artifact is
# withheld from StageFreight's publish stage until the substrate-pull
# repair fires.
#
# The body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation reads
# the movement's discharged state, consumes the family-root's
# `song_settles` verdict, decides the StageFreight cascade dispatch
# (publish + narrate on Splinter-pole; withhold on Narcissus-pole),
# emits the closed movement ref. The substrate declares the species-
# altitude specialisation; consumers dispatch through the species
# boundary.
close(m: song_movement, p: perturbation) -> song_movement { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The out clauses
# ============================================================

out @song/movement
out song_movement
out enter
out close
